Turns off draft 32's expiry of exclusions (commit 7a62e61, DESIGN.md
§7.5): `WantList::expire` no longer releases an exclusion whose backoff has
run out, and `next_deadline` no longer counts its expiry, so the engine asks
for no wake-up for it. A source excluded after one corrupted transfer is
then released only by draft 31's events (it reconnecting, a batch
announcing the wanted content at the path, or the index at the path
changing), and a want whose only source stays connected and silent waits
for it to the end of the run.

test: delocal-sim regressions::an_exclusion_expires_for_a_conflict_copy
test: delocal-engine want::tests::an_exclusion_expires_on_a_backoff_that_doubles_per_source
test: delocal-engine want::tests::a_give_up_expires_with_its_first_exclusion

